{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Investigate three areas, using daily fund and benchmark returns on the same dates, with distributions, fees and benchmark conventions treated consistently:\n\n- **Portfolio:** incomplete or delayed index rebalances; sampling/optimization choices; cash drag or flows; corporate actions; withholding taxes; securities-lending income; derivatives, collateral and counterparty effects; and constraints or trading that leave the portfolio off-index.\n- **Pricing and measurement:** stale or asynchronous security prices, fair-value adjustments, market- versus NAV-based fund returns, bid–ask spreads, premiums/discounts, FX timing (if relevant), benchmark return methodology, and data or calendar mismatches. These can create apparent volatility even without a persistent portfolio shortfall.\n- **Operations:** trade or corporate-action processing errors, incorrect holdings or cash, fee accruals, delayed subscriptions/redemptions, settlement issues, and errors in NAV or benchmark data feeds.\n\nDecompose the daily active-return series and compare with prior periods and peers; separately assess cumulative tracking difference, which measures total return shortfall or excess, not variability."}}
